      <activity id="0c87e66b-763d-5e36-914f-509d9d88d5de" activityNameId="88b73257-41f3-5cc1-990e-2202194d1f09" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural gas, production TH, at long-distance pipeline</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural gas, production TH, at long-distance pipeline
In 2023 100% of the imported Thai natural gas to GLO was imported by pipeline and 0% as LNG. An average distance of 0 km is estimated for the pipeline export from Thailand, of which are 0 km offshore pipeline. The estimated shipping distance for LNG are  km. The net calorific value of natural is 36.0 MJ/Nm³. UUID=3121dcba-7ccc-3c66-b5be-50377ff67ef1
This dataset describes the transport needed for an average export of Thai natural gas. Gas losses and emissions during seasonal storage are included.
Location: The data for storage emissions are based on global data. The amount of gas stored is a rough estimate based on European data. The average weighted transport distance is based on the trade movements 2019.
Technology: The distance is an European average based on the European long-distance pipeline network and LNG shipping routes.
Time period: Transport modes investigated for 2023.
Production volume: not known
Sampling: Literature.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_3121dcba-7ccc-3c66-b5be-50377ff67ef1.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
